******What is the OSI Model?

OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) is a 7-layer reference model that explains how data is transmitted from one computer to another over a network.
It is called a reference model because it serves as a guideline for designing and understanding network communication.

Interview Definition ⭐
The OSI Model is a seven-layer framework that standardizes network communication by dividing the communication process into seven different layers, each with a specific responsibility.

****OSI Layers
7. Application
6. Presentation
5. Session
4. Transport
3. Network
2. Data Link
1. Physical



******1---Application Layer
The Application Layer is the layer through which users communicate with the network using applications like web browsers, email clients, and messaging apps.
The Application Layer is responsible for providing network services to user applications so that users can send and receive data over a network.
Real-Life Example

When you open:

Chrome
Gmail
WhatsApp
Instagram

You are using the Application Layer.

Responsibilities
Web browsing
Email
File transfer
Remote login
Protocols
HTTP
HTTPS
FTP
SMTP
DNS
Interview Answer

The Application Layer provides network services directly to end-user applications.



2-----Layer 6 — Presentation Layer
Definition
This layer changes the format of data so both sender and receiver understand it.

Think of it as a translator.
Responsibilities

1. Encryption
Plain Text
↓
Encrypted Text

2. Decryption
Encrypted Text
↓
Plain Text

3. Compression
Large file
↓
Small file

4. Translation
Different data formats
↓
Common format

Real-Life Example

HTTPS encrypts your data before sending it.

Interview Answer

The Presentation Layer handles encryption, decryption, compression, and translation of data.

Layer 5 — Session Layer
Definition
Creates,
Maintains,
Ends communication sessions.

Example

Google Meet
When you join,
A session starts.
When you leave,
The session ends.

Responsibilities
Session establishment
Session maintenance
Session termination
Interview Answer

The Session Layer manages communication sessions between two devices.


4. Transport Layer (Layer 4) ⭐⭐⭐ (Most Important)

This is one of the most frequently asked interview topics.
Purpose
Provides end-to-end communication.

Ensures that data reaches the receiver correctly.

Responsibilities
Segmentation

Large files are divided into small pieces called segments.

Reassembly

Receiver joins the segments again.

Error Detection

Detects lost or corrupted data.

Flow Control

Prevents a fast sender from overwhelming a slow receiver.

Reliable Delivery

Ensures data arrives correctly (using TCP).

Protocols
TCP

Reliable

Connection-oriented

Slow

UDP

Fast

Connectionless

No delivery guarantee


*******Network Layer (Layer 3) – Short Notes (Placement Revision)
Definition
Responsible for routing data from source to destination.
Uses IP Address to identify devices.
Finds the best path for data transmission.
Main Functions
✅ Logical Addressing (IP Address)
✅ Routing (Best Path Selection)
✅ Packet Forwarding
✅ Packet Delivery (Best-Effort)
Uses
Address Used: IP Address
Device: Router
Data Unit: Packet
Layer Number: 3
Protocols
IP (Internet Protocol) ⭐
ICMP
IGMP
IPsec
Important Facts ⭐
Router works at the Network Layer.
Uses IP Address (Logical Address).
Data Unit = Packet.
Performs Routing.
IP is Connectionless.
IP provides Best-Effort Delivery (No guarantee).
Interview Questions

Q1. What is the main function of the Network Layer?

Routing and logical addressing.

Q2. Which address is used by the Network Layer?

IP Address.

Q3. Which device works at the Network Layer?

Router.

Q4. What is the data unit of the Network Layer?

Packet.

Q5. Which protocol works at the Network Layer?

IP (Internet Protocol).


********Data Link Layer (Layer 2) – Easy Notes (Placement)
What is the Data Link Layer?

The Data Link Layer is responsible for sending data between two devices on the same local network (LAN).
It uses the MAC Address to identify devices.

Simple Definition ⭐
The Data Link Layer transfers data between devices on the same network using MAC addresses.

Main Functions
1. Physical Addressing

Uses MAC Address.

Example:

00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E

Every network card has a MAC address.

2. Framing

The Data Link Layer converts Packets into Frames.

Network Layer
Packet
      ↓
Data Link Layer
Frame
3. Error Detection

Checks if data is corrupted during transmission.

If an error is detected, the receiver knows the frame is damaged.

4. Local Delivery

Delivers data within the same network (LAN).

Important Terms
MAC Address
Physical Address
Usually fixed
48-bit
Used inside a LAN
Frame

Data unit of the Data Link Layer.

Device

Switch

Placement Facts ⭐
Layer Number = 2
Address Used = MAC Address
Device = Switch
Data Unit = Frame
Used for communication within the same network (LAN)
Interview Questions
Q1. What is the main function of the Data Link Layer?

Answer: It transfers data between devices on the same network using MAC addresses.

Q2. Which address is used?

Answer: MAC Address.

Q3. Which device works here?

Answer: Switch.

Q4. What is the data unit?

Answer: Frame.


*******Physical Layer (Layer 1) – Easy Notes
What is the Physical Layer?

The Physical Layer is the lowest layer of the OSI model.
It is responsible for actually sending bits (0s and 1s) through cables, optical fiber, or wireless signals.

Simple Definition ⭐
The Physical Layer transmits raw bits (0s and 1s) over the physical communication medium.

Real-Life Example
Imagine you are talking to your friend on a phone call.
Your voice travels through:

Mobile tower
Radio waves
Fiber cables

Similarly,

Computers send electrical, optical, or wireless signals through the Physical Layer.

Example
Laptop
   │
LAN Cable
   │
Switch

The cable carries only 0s and 1s (bits).

The Physical Layer is responsible for sending these bits.

Main Functions
1. Transmits Bits
Sends data as:
010101010101
These are called Bits.

2. Defines Transmission Medium

Examples:

LAN Cable
Optical Fiber
Wi-Fi Signals
Radio Waves

3. Signal Conversion
Converts bits into:

Electrical signals
Optical signals
Wireless signals

for transmission.

Devices
Hub
Repeater
Cables
Fiber Optic
Data Unit

Bits

Placement Facts ⭐
Layer Number = 1
Data Unit = Bits
Devices = Hub, Repeater
Works with cables and signals
Lowest layer of the OSI model
Interview Questions
Q1. What is the job of the Physical Layer?
Answer: It transmits raw bits over the communication medium.

Q2. What is the data unit?
Answer: Bits.

Q3. Which devices work here?
Answer: Hub and Repeater.





